    {
      "review_id": "18545",
      "reviewer_name": "Michael",
      "reviewer_location": "QLD - 4701",
      "reviewer_state": "QLD",
      "reviewer_postcode": "4701",
      "reviewer_postcode_valid": true,
      "review_date": "2013-05-07",
      "review_date_formatted": "",
      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "Solartech Energy Solutions  provided the most informative, prompt comprehensive site inspection without sales pitch of all of the 9 installers/sellerswe contacted.  Gave us a full list of base system options from 2kW to 5kW and options regarding installation location for the panels and inverter, provided area based irradiation figures - daily and percentage against inclination, and a list of 40 biggest panel manufacturers.  They only dealt with Trina/Suntech panels and Sunnyboy/Power One inverters. Suntech was going through a restructure at the time, so Trina TSM-PC05A.08 250W panels with a 3.0kw Power One inverter for $6016 was our preferred option.  Due to competition I was able to renegotiate to $5835.  This system was installed on the 24th April 2013, 5 weeks after site inspection. We had an earlier install (3 weeks) due to other buyers not being exactly ready for an install.Installation went for about 5 hours without a fuss and looks very clean and tidy. Team of 4 were efficient,  tidy and polite. They also thanked us for the business and gave helpful advice on top of the required info regarding the operation and maintenance of the system.The other local  installer we seriously considered were Infinity Solar. Conducted site inspection that was informative and without sales pitch. Provided me with inverter and panel information and installation options.Very competitive on the quote for a 3kW system Power One 3.0 kw/ 12 Trina TSM-PC05A 250W at $6490. Due to competition for the 3kW Trina/Power One combo in QLD they did come down to $6146 and then $5835.All other quotes from other installers/sellers involved information that:was diffcult to confirm/correlate with others, orwas overpriced (one installer quoted a buget Jinko panel /Samil inverter system that was $1600 more than the Trina/PVI we obtained), orprice limited to metroploitan areas, such as Brisbane, Sydney, Melbourne, ordelivered with sales pitch, orsales service was lacking.",
